parameters.body/message:
Classify the following input into one of these categories: Actionable request, Noise, Other

Category definitions:
- Actionable request: A genuine human-authored request that requires review or action. Includes requests for help, access, onboarding, invoices, payments, sales inquiries, technical support, facilities, approvals, questions, or other business services. Select this category only when the sender is asking for information, assistance, or an action. Do not select it for automated messages, acknowledgments, notifications, newsletters, delivery reports, or unsubscribe requests.
- Noise: An automated, non-actionable, or irrelevant email that should not enter request triage. Includes out-of-office or absence notices; automatic replies and acknowledgments; vacation responses; delivery status notifications, bounce messages, and undeliverable reports; read receipts; mailbox notifications; system-generated alerts with no request for action; newsletters, marketing, promotions, and mailing-list messages; unsubscribe or subscription-management requests; spam; empty messages; and messages that merely confirm receipt. Select this category when the email does not contain a genuine human request requiring business action.

Input to classify: Subject: @{triggerOutputs()?['body/subject']} 
From: @{triggerOutputs()?['body/from']} 
Body: @{triggerOutputs()?['body/body']} 

Respond with only the category name. If the input does not clearly match any of the categories, respond with "Other".
